  "configuration_id": "config_044",
  "reason": "Evidence: Multiprofile + scvi_n200 is clearly the strongest backbone (config_002: 0.650, config_007: 0.653), but adding resnet50 image features in the multimodal multiprofile setting (config_037: 0.632) actually *hurts* relative to RNA-only. Image-only with resnet50 is very weak (0.208), suggesting resnet50 features may be the bottleneck rather than the image modality itself. Uncertainty: We have not tested whether a stronger, pretrained image encoder (imagenet_vit_l) can produce representations that actually complement the RNA profile. Question: config_044 (multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, concat) is a clean single-variable swap of the image encoder from resnet50 → imagenet_vit_l relative to config_037, while matching the aggregation (avgpool) and fusion (concat) of the best RNA-only multiprofile baseline. This isolates the effect of image encoder quality. Why best next experiment: If config_044 exceeds config_037 and approaches or beats config_002, it reveals the image modality has untapped value with a better encoder, justifying further multimodal exploration. If it still lags behind RNA-only, it provides strong evidence that the image channel is not useful for this task, allowing us to focus remaining budget on RNA-only multiprofile refinements (aggregation, encoder variants). Either outcome significantly reduces uncertainty about a core design axis (representation/fusion) with a single clean comparison."
}

